{"caveats":"Same ordinance and overlapping period, but not matched bargaining-unit contracts: the Chief was outside the police bargaining unit, and role/rank/hours/schedule equivalence with the Administrative Assistant is unverified. Use only as bounded local documentary evidence after manual/legal/substantive validation, not as a final wage-gap estimate.","claim_boundary":"conditional_with_caveats","claim_family":"local_comparison","municipality":"Alburtis","no_causal_claim":true,"no_final_national_claim":true,"original_record_id":"B4X2500GAP-41d42064465db4099b779674","pay_basis":"hourly","qa_status":"conditional_example_ready","source_layer":"BROAD-STATE-4X2500-BOUNDED-WAGE-DIFFERENTIAL-VALIDATION-2026-07-30","state":"PA","unit_type":"local_comparison","whole_corpus_claim_record_id":"WCCR-9aad877c35b4dd3418736db8"}
{"caveats":"Same-page hourly maximum schedule values and arithmetic are validated, but Section 2 permits actual salaries below the maxima and the council-packet copy has blank adoption/approval fields; use only as a bounded local comparison of listed maximum rates pending manual/legal validation.","claim_boundary":"conditional_with_caveats","claim_family":"local_comparison","municipality":"Cammack Village","no_causal_claim":true,"no_final_national_claim":true,"original_record_id":"B4X2500GAP-4193e4d9ff2676c7d2680e77","pay_basis":"hourly","qa_status":"conditional_example_ready","source_layer":"BROAD-STATE-4X2500-BOUNDED-WAGE-DIFFERENTIAL-VALIDATION-2026-07-30","state":"AR","unit_type":"local_comparison","whole_corpus_claim_record_id":"WCCR-3aadfe08c34263aa12d46d94"}
{"caveats":"The police value is specifically the Year 1 entry step for officers hired after 1999, while the Code Enforcement Officer line provides a single listed rate with no tenure, step, or experience label. The source establishes common municipality, cycle, page, hourly pay basis, and schedule-listed wage status, but it does not establish comparable tenure, experience, duties, qualifications, hours, full-time status, or schedule position. The upstream normalized Code Enforcement Officer record was incorrectly tagged as police; this validation corrects the candidate interpretation from the verbatim source line but does not overwrite the raw upstream record. The negative $0.91/hour documentary difference pertains only to these two specifically listed schedule values and must not be generalized to police and non-safety employees in Canastota. This is bounded local documentary evidence, not a final wage-gap estimate, and is not nationally representative. Substantive/manual validation of occupational and schedule-position comparability is required before analytic use beyond a qualified supporting example.","claim_boundary":"conditional_with_caveats","claim_family":"local_comparison","municipality":"Canastota","no_causal_claim":true,"no_final_national_claim":true,"original_record_id":"B4X2500GAP-498d2fdd8da985bf2455ab27","pay_basis":"hourly","qa_status":"conditional_example_ready","source_layer":"BROAD-STATE-4X2500-BOUNDED-WAGE-DIFFERENTIAL-VALIDATION-2026-07-30","state":"NY","unit_type":"local_comparison","whole_corpus_claim_record_id":"WCCR-0fdd0a6225db601d65e302a6"}
